# Local development environment. There is nothing here to copy into `.env` any more, and saying so is
# the whole point of keeping the file: this is where you would look first.
#
# The one variable this file ever set, `PUBLIC_SPEC`, pinned a build to a single spec through
# `import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SPEC`. It went away when the site became one build serving every spec by
# route — `/monk/windwalker`, `/shaman/elemental`, a splash at `/`. A spec is chosen by visiting its
# route, so there is no build-time default left to set and nothing for Astro to inline.
#
# The two variables below do still exist. They are listed here because this is the file people look
# in for them, and with the warning that setting them here does nothing at all.

# --- not read from `.env`; listed for reference -----------------------------------------------
# Canonical site URL and path prefix, consumed by `astro.config.mjs`.
#
# `astro.config.mjs` reads them from the real process environment (`process.env`), which is not the
# channel Astro loads this file into. Export them in the shell (`SITE_URL=… npm run build`) or leave
# them to their defaults. The deploy sets them in a workflow `env:` block
# (`.github/workflows/deploy-cloudflare.yml`), never from a file.
#
# Cloudflare Pages is what a push to `main` publishes: one project, one host, at the root of its own
# domain, so there is no prefix:
#   SITE_URL=https://mop-log-analyzer.pages.dev
#   BASE_PATH=
#
# GitHub Pages needs both, because a project site is served under `/<repo>/` and an unprefixed build
# 404s every asset:
#   SITE_URL=https://1337lutz.github.io
#   BASE_PATH=/windwalker-analyzer
#
# `npm run dev` sets neither, so it serves at `http://localhost:4321/` with no prefix. Writing
# `BASE_PATH` here will not change that, for the reason above.
#
# Moving the site means registering the new URL with WarcraftLogs as a redirect URI. It is matched
# byte for byte, and an unregistered one fails as `invalid_client`, which reads as a wrong client id
# and is not. The move to `mop-log-analyzer.pages.dev` is exactly that move, for every existing user
# at once — see `docs/wcl-oauth.md`.
